abstract: >
  NyayaChain is a permissioned blockchain system for recording and verifying
  court-ordered property freeze orders on tokenized land records. Built on
  Hyperledger Besu with a 4-node QBFT consensus cluster, it performs 11–12
  sequential on-chain verification checks per freeze/unfreeze order, including
  ECDSA signature validation, territorial jurisdiction, judicial key validity
  windows, and sequential nonce enforcement. The system demonstrates
  sub-2.1-second median confirmation latency for a three-signer quorum on a
  local permissioned network.
